euphemism vs dysphemism
418.3 Semantics & pragmatics

TYPE      euphemism
VALUE     polite_term(impolite_thing)
EXAMPLE   "let go"          → fired
          "love handles"    → waist fat
          "powder room"     → toilet

TYPE      dysphemism
VALUE     impolite_term(polite_thing)
EXAMPLE   "rawdogging"      → winging it
          "rug rat"         → child
          "beak"            → nose

FUNDAMENTALS
  both replace a direct word
  euphemism softens
  dysphemism sharpens
  same referent, opposite tone
